      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e so probably we can add below in kvm_pkvm_hypercalls.h, to define PKVM_HC_INOUT as PKVM_HC if it is not defined.\n\nYeah, seems like a good idea.\n\n\u003e With the new name pkvm_hypercall, maybe also rename this handler to pkvm_handle_host_hypercalls()?\n\nYeah, makes sense. Probably just pkvm_handle_host_hypercall() (singular, not plural)?\n\nBTW also just a note: IOMMU hypercalls are actually Intel (VT-d) specific, so in v6.18, their definitions should be probably under #ifdef CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL, and their handling should be probably not directly in generic pkvm_handle_host_hypercall() but somewhere e.g. in arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/iommu.c?",
